        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b71e724c-2911-5ee9-93bd-2cc7a235a3e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Rendezvous Music, Rendezvous Entertainment, Mack Avenue Records\n- People: Dave Koz, Frank Cody, Hyman Katz, Kirk Whalum, Jonathan Butler, Kyle Eastwood, Wayman Tisdale\n- Places: University of Oklahoma\n- Organizations: RIAA, National Collegiate Basketball Hall of Fame\n- Topics: Record labels, music releases, basketball, smooth jazz\n\nFacts:\n- Rendezvous Music, formerly known as Rendezvous Entertainment, was founded in 2002 by Dave Koz, Frank Cody, and Hyman Katz.\n- Wayman Tisdale was born on June 9, 1964, and he was an American NBA basketball player and smooth jazz bass guitarist.\n- Rendezvous Music became part of the Mack Avenue Records label group after its acquisition in August 2008.\n- Rendezvous Music continued releasing new music by Kirk Whalum, Jonathan Butler, and Kyle Eastwood, as well as previously unreleased music by Wayman Tisdale, after joining Mack Avenue Records.\n- Wayman Tisdale was elected to the National Collegiate Basketball Hall of Fame in 2009 after being a three-time All-American at the University of Oklahoma.\n- Wayman Tisdale died on May 15, 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
